Z||000000||fierovette||06-23-2001||08:30 AM||||I found the pressure sender,(thanks to all your help out there)I disconnected the three wire plug, and the gage is still at max when you turn on the ing.I was told that the sending unit is OK if this happends. Is it the gage? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-23-2001||08:42 AM||||My experience 2 Fieros and 3 oil sending units each (all V6), it is the sending unit or the connection to the sending unit.<P>The oil guage pegs.<P>I had the three wire plug to the sending unit replaced, the sending unit was a week old, but the plug was bad and shorted out the sending unit.  Make sure the sending unit has the "water proof" grommet in place.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||varnster||06-23-2001||10:34 PM||||I changed mine 2 weeks ago and performed same test and yes the guage pegs, thats what<BR>it does for some reason {electrical junk}<BR>go ahead and change it, you will be fine<BR>afterward, take a look at the historicals<BR>their is some good info their.||||reg||1
